olleagues. Candidate C can make correct decisions quickly, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe need to discuss candidate C's concerns and compare with others. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate B's uncooperative behavior (makes nasty remarks) is a serious crew cooperation issue, making C still preferable. Or we could raise that Candidate D's hot temper and know-it-all attitude may be problematic. Or we could ask for more info about Candidate C's stress resilience beyond crisis calm.\n\nWe could also ask a tool question to another agent for more info about Candidate C's stress handling. But we have a fact: C keeps calm in a crisis. That addresses stress resilience somewhat. But we might want to ask about other stress scenarios.\n\nBut the instruction: we should make a public contribution, not a tool call, unless we need missing info. We could ask a tool call to Agent 1 for more details on C's stress handling. However we already have \"keeps calm in a crisis\". Might be enough.\n\nWe need to give our vote. We could either agree with Agent 1 (vote C) or propose another candidate. Let's evaluate: Candidate C has strong reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Candidate B is conscientious, handles stress, but makes nasty remarks (crew cooperation). Candidate A has technical strengths but not open to new ideas, show-off, maybe reliability issues. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nThus C still seems best overall. We can agree with Agent 1, but note concerns and suggest we need to verify communication and adaptability. We can ask for more info on C's willingness to accept feedback (adaptability). Could ask Agent 1 or 3.\n\nBut we need to produce a public message now. We can say: I agree with Candidate C as leading, but we need to probe communication and egocentric concerns. Provide evidence: reliability, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere. Mention that compared to B's nasty remarks, C's crew atmosphere is better. Also note that A's show-off and not open to new ideas may affect adaptability. D's hot temper also problematic.\n\nThus we keep vote C.\n\nWe must include metadata JSON with vote \"Candidate C\".\n\nProceed."}
