mplex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities) and note concerns (show-off, not open to new ideas). Compare with C's communication issues. Could argue that A's technical competence and leadership may outweigh C's communication concerns, but his lack of openness to new ideas is a problem for adaptability. We could ask for any observations on A's reliability or crew cooperation. But we need to keep one focused contribution.\n\nGiven the SMM, we should consider next move: Candidate A is still under-discussed. We have strengths not yet discussed. So we could bring up Candidate A's strengths and ask about reliability/crew cooperation. That would move discussion forward. Also we could keep our vote maybe still C, but we could say we remain with C but want more info on A. Or we could shift to A if we think his strengths outweigh C's concerns. Let's evaluate: A has strong technical competence (anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership). But concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas. No info on reliability, stress resilience, crew cooperation. So we lack evidence. C has strong reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty. Which is more critical? Probably reliability and crew cooperation are top. C's communication difficulty could be mitigated with training. A's unknown reliability is a risk. So likely still C.\n\nThus we can keep vote C, but bring up Candidate A's strengths and request missing info (reliability, crew cooperation). That aligns with covering all candidates.\n\nWe need to produce public message: \"I agree with C, but we still need to evaluate A's reliability and crew cooperation. Based on my notes, A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but is seen as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas. These strengths could be valuable, but the concerns raise questions about adaptability and teamwork. Do we have any observations on A's operational reliability or how he works with crew?\" That would be a focused contribution, referencing discussion, providing evidence, and asking a question.\n\nWe need to include metadata JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
